    "text": "SYN Flooding Attack: Va > A malicious attacker sends a large number of SYN segments to a server, pretending that each of them is coming from a different client by faking the source IP addresses in the datagrams. > Server allocates the necessary resources and sends the SYN +ACK segments to the fake clients, which are lost. > Ifthe number of SYN segments is large, server runs out of resources and may crash. > This is a denial-of-service attack as server denies any further service to every forthcoming request. Preventive Strategies: eaposing a limit on connection requests during a specified period of time. > , Per out datagrams coming from unwanted source addresses. » Kostpone resource allocation until the entire connection Is set up.",
